Lex["0582"] = "'enowsh {en-oshe'}|AV - man 520, certain 10, husbands 3, some 3, merchantmen 2,<BR>persons 2, misc 24; 564|from 0605|TWOT - 136a|noun masculine| INDENT0--<b>1)</b> man, mortal man, person, mankind INDENT3--<b>a)</b> of an individual INDENT3--<b>b)</b> men (collective) INDENT3--<b>c)</b> man, mankind <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1488;&#1457;&#1504;&#1493;&#1465;&#1513;&#1473; </span>&#700;&#277;n&#244;wsh, en-oshe'; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=605&page=1\">H605</a>; properly, a mortal (and thus differing from the more dignified 120); hence, a man in general (singly or collectively):&#8212;another, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> (blood-) thirsty, certain, chap(-man); divers, fellow, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> in the flower of their age, husband, (certain, mortal) man, people, person, servant, some (<sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> of them), stranger, those, their trade. It is often unexpressed in the English versions, especially when used in apposition with another word. Compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=376&page=1\">H376</a>.";
