Lex["01235"] = "beqa` {beh'-kah}|AV - half a shekel 1, bekah 1; 2|from 01234|TWOT - 271a|noun masculine| INDENT0--<b>1)</b> half, part also called \"shekel of the sanctuary\" or \"holy shekel\" INDENT0--<b>2)</b> half a shekel (meton) There appears to be at least three different shekels, one of silver, gold and copper. See a Bible Dictionary for a complete treatment of the subject. <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1489;&#1468;&#1462;&#1511;&#1463;&#1506; </span>  beqa&#699;, beh&#39;-kah; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=1234&page=1\">H1234</a>; a section (half) of a shekel, i.e. a beka (a weight and a coin):&#8212;bekah, half a shekel.";
