Lex["02603"] = "chanan {khaw-nan'}|AV - mercy 16, gracious 13, merciful 12, supplication 10, favour 7,<BR>besought 4, pity 4, fair 1, favourable 1, favoured 1, misc 9; 78|a primitive root [compare 02583]|TWOT - 694,695|verb| INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to be gracious, show favour, pity INDENT3--<b>a)</b> (Qal) to show favour, be gracious INDENT3--<b>b)</b> (Niphal) to be pitied INDENT3--<b>c)</b> (Piel) to make gracious, make favourable, be gracious INDENT3--<b>d)</b> (Poel) to direct favour to, have mercy on INDENT3--<b>e)</b> (Hophal) to be shown favour, be shown consideration INDENT3--<b>f)</b> (Hithpael) to seek favour, implore favour INDENT0--<b>2)</b> to be loathsome <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1495;&#1464;&#1504;&#1463;&#1503; </span>  ch&#226;nan, khaw-nan&#39;; a primitive root (compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=2583&page=1\">H2583</a>); properly, to bend or stoop in kindness to an inferior; to favor, bestow; causatively to implore (i.e. move to favor by petition):&#8212;beseech, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> fair, (be, find, shew) favour(-able), be (deal, give, grant (gracious(-ly), intreat, (be) merciful, have (shew) mercy (on, upon), have pity upon, pray, make supplication, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> very.";
