Lex["03003"] = "Yabesh {yaw-bashe'}|AV - Jabesh 12, Jabeshgilead 12; 24|the same as 03002 (also Yabeysh {yaw-bashe'})||noun proper locative, noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Jabesh = \"dry\"<br><br> INDENT0--noun proper locative<BR> INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a town in the territory of Gilead; according to Eusebius, it is beyond the Jordan, 6 miles (10 km) from Pella, on the mountain road to Gerasa; site unknown but may be modern 'Wadi Yabes'<br><br> INDENT0--noun proper masculine<BR> INDENT0--<b>2)</b> father of Shallum, the 15th king of the northern kingdom <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1497;&#1464;&#1489;&#1461;&#1513;&#1473; </span> Y&#226;b&#234;sh, yaw-bashe&#39;; the same as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=3002&page=1\">H3002</a> (also <span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1497;&#1464;&#1489;&#1461;&#1497;&#1513;&#1473; </span> Y&#xE2;b&#xEA;ysh; often with the addition of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=1568&page=1\">H1568</a>, i.e. Jabesh of Gilad); Jobesh, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine:&#8212;Jobesh (-Gilead).";
