Lex["03220"] = "yam {yawm}|AV - sea 321, west 47, westward 21, west side 4, seafaring men 1,<BR>south 1, western 1; 396|from an unused root meaning to roar|TWOT - 871a|noun masculine| INDENT0--<b>1)</b> sea INDENT3--<b>a)</b> Mediterranean Sea INDENT3--<b>b)</b> Red Sea INDENT3--<b>c)</b> Dead Sea INDENT3--<b>d)</b> Sea of Galilee INDENT3--<b>e)</b> sea (general) INDENT3--<b>f)</b> mighty river (Nile) INDENT3--<b>g)</b> the sea (the great basin in the temple court) INDENT3--<b>h)</b> seaward, west, westward <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1497;&#1464;&#1501;</span>  y&#226;m, yawm; from an unused root meaning to roar; a sea (as breaking in noisy surf) or large body of water; specifically (with the article), the Mediterranean Sea; sometimes a large river, or an artifical basin; locally, the west, or (rarely) the south:&#8212;sea (<sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> -faring man, (-shore)), south, west (-ern, side, -ward).";
