Lex["03651"] = "ken {kane}|AV - so, thus, like manner, well, such thing, howbeit, state, after<BR>that, following, after this, therefore, wherefore, surely; 42|from 03559|TWOT - 964a,964b|adverb, adjective| INDENT0--adverb<BR> INDENT0--<b>1)</b> so, therefore, thus INDENT3--<b>a)</b> thus, so INDENT3--<b>b)</b> just so INDENT3--<b>c)</b> therefore<BR> INDENT3--<b>d)</b> so...as (paired with adverb) INDENT3--<b>e)</b> then INDENT3--<b>f)</b> forasmuch as (in phrase) INDENT3--<b>g)</b> (with preposition) INDENT7--<b>1)</b> therefore, this being so (specific) INDENT7--<b>2)</b> hitherto INDENT7--<b>3)</b> therefore, on this ground (general) INDENT7--<b>4)</b> afterwards INDENT7--<b>5)</b> in such case<br><br> INDENT0--adjective<BR> INDENT0--<b>2)</b> right, just, honest, true, veritable INDENT3--<b>a)</b> right, just, honest INDENT3--<b>b)</b> correct INDENT3--<b>c)</b> true, veritable INDENT3--<b>d)</b> true!, right!, correct! (in assent) <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1499;&#1468;&#1461;&#1503;</span> k&#234;n, kane; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=3559&page=1\">H3559</a>; properly, set upright; hence (figuratively as adjective) just; but usually (as adverb or conjunction) rightly or so (in various applications to manner, time and relation; often with other particles):&#8212; after that (this, -ward, -wards), as... as, (for-) asmuch as yet, be (for which) cause, following, howbeit, in (the) like (manner, -wise), <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> the more, right, (even) so, state, straightway, such (thing), surely, there (where) -fore, this, thus, true, well, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> you.";
