Lex["04911"] = "mashal {maw-shal'}|AV - like 5, proverb 4, speak 2, use 2, become 1, compare 1, utter 1; 16|denominative from 04912|TWOT - 1258,1258b|verb| INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to represent, liken, be like INDENT3--<b>a)</b> (Niphal) to liken, be like, be similar INDENT3--<b>b)</b> (Hiphil) to compare INDENT3--<b>c)</b> (Hithpael) to become like INDENT0--<b>2)</b> to speak in a proverb, use a proverb, speak in parables, speak in sentences of poetry INDENT3--<b>a)</b> (Qal) to use a proverb, speak a parable or proverb INDENT3--<b>b)</b> (Piel) to make a parable INDENT7--<b>1)</b> maker of parables (participle) <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1502;&#1464;&#1513;&#1473;&#1463;&#1500; </span> m&#226;shal, maw-shal&#39;; denominative from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=4912&page=1\">H4912</a>; to liken, i.e. (transitively) to use figurative language (an allegory, adage, song or the like); intransitively, to resemble:&#8212;be(-come) like, compare, use (as a) proverb, speak (in proverbs), utter.";
