Lex["05015"] = "N@bow {neb-o'}|AV - Nebo 13; 13|probably of foreign derivation|TWOT - 1279,1280|noun proper masculine, noun proper locative| INDENT0--Nebo = \"prophet\"<br><br> INDENT0--noun proper masculine<BR> INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a Babylonian deity who presided over learning and letters; corresponds to Greek Hermes, Latin Mercury, and Egyptian Thoth<br><br> INDENT0--noun proper locative<BR> INDENT0--<b>2)</b> a city in Moab and at one time assigned to Reuben; probably located on or near Mount Nebo INDENT0--<b>3)</b> a city in Judah (maybe Benjamin) from which the families of some exiles, who returned from Babylon with Zerubbabel, originally came INDENT0--<b>4)</b> the mountain where Moses died; located east of the Jordan opposite Jericho; site uncertain <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1504;&#1456;&#1489;&#1493;&#1465; </span> N&#7497;b&#244;w, neb-o&#39;; probably of foreign derivation; Nebo, the name of a Babylonian deity, also of a mountain in Moab, and of a place in Palestine:&#8212;Nebo.";
