Lex["05324"] = "natsab {naw-tsab'}|AV - stand 34, set 12, officers 6, set up 7, upright 2, appointed 1,<BR>deputy 1, erected 1, establish 1, Huzzab 1, misc 9; 75|A primitive root|TWOT - 1398|verb| INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to stand, take one's stand, stand upright, be set (over), establish INDENT3--<b>a)</b> (Niphal) INDENT7--<b>1)</b> to station oneself, take one's stand INDENT7--<b>2)</b> to stand, be stationed INDENT7--<b>3)</b> to stand, take an upright position INDENT7--<b>4)</b> to be stationed, be appointed INDENT7--<b>5)</b> deputy, prefect, appointed, deputed (substantive) INDENT7--<b>6)</b> to stand firm INDENT3--<b>b)</b> (Hiphil) INDENT7--<b>1)</b> to station, set INDENT7--<b>2)</b> to set up, erect INDENT7--<b>3)</b> to cause to stand erect INDENT7--<b>4)</b> to fix, establish INDENT3--<b>c)</b> (Hophal) to be fixed, be determined, be stationary <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1504;&#1464;&#1510;&#1463;&#1489; </span> n&#226;tsab, naw-tsab&#39;; a primitive root; to station, in various applications (literally or figuratively):&#8212;appointed, deputy, erect, establish, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> Huzzah (by mistake for a proper name), lay, officer, pillar, present, rear up, set (over, up), settle, sharpen, establish, (make to) stand(-ing, still, up, upright), best state.";
