Lex["06271"] = "`Athalyah {ath-al-yaw'} or `Athalyahuw {ath-al-yaw'-hoo}|AV - Athaliah 17; 17|from the same as 06270 and 03050||noun proper masculine, noun proper feminine| INDENT0--Athaliah = \"afflicted of the Lord\"<BR><br> INDENT0--noun proper masculine<BR> INDENT0--<b>1)</b> son of Jeroham of the tribe of Benjamin INDENT0--<b>2)</b> father of Jeshaiah of the sons of Elam who was one of the heads of a family who returned with Ezra from exile<br><br> INDENT0--noun proper feminine<BR> INDENT0--<b>3)</b> the daughter of Ahab and Jezebel and the wife of king Jehoram of Judah; killer of all the members of the royal family of Judah with the exception of one baby named Joash who was hidden by the high-priest Jehoiada until 6 years had passed and Jehoiada led the revolution to put him on the throne, overthrowing Athaliah and putting her to death <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1506;&#1458;&#1514;&#1463;&#1500;&#1456;&#1497;&#1464;&#1492; </span> &#699;&#259;thaly&#226;h, ath-al-yaw&#39;; or <span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1506;&#1458;&#1514;&#1463;&#1500;&#1456;&#1497;&#1464;&#1492;&#1493;&#1468;</span>  &#x2BB;&#x102;thaly&#xE2;h&#xFB;w; from the same as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=6270&page=1\">H6270</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=3050&page=1\">H3050</a>; Jah has constrained; Athaljah, the name of an Israelitess and two Israelites:&#8212;Athaliah.";
