Lex["06310"] = "peh {peh} or pim {pim}|AV - mouth 340, commandment 37, edge 35, according 22, word 15, hole 6,<BR>end 3, appointment 2, portion 2, tenor 2, sentence 2, misc 32; 498|from 06284|TWOT - 1738|noun masculine| INDENT0--<b>1)</b> (peh) mouth INDENT3--<b>a)</b> mouth (of man) INDENT3--<b>b)</b> mouth (as organ of speech) INDENT3--<b>c)</b> mouth (of animals) INDENT3--<b>d)</b> mouth, opening, orifice (of a well, river, etc) INDENT3--<b>e)</b> extremity, end INDENT0--<b>2)</b> (pim) a weight equal to one third of a shekel, occurs only in 1 Sa. 13:21 <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1508;&#1468;&#1462;&#1492; </span> peh, peh; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=6284&page=1\">H6284</a>; the mouth (as the means of blowing), whether literal or figurative (particularly speech); specifically edge, portion or side; adverbially (with preposition) according to:&#8212;accord(-ing as, -ing to), after, appointment, assent, collar, command(-ment), <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> eat, edge, end, entry, file, hole, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> in, mind, mouth, part, portion, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> (should) say(-ing), sentence, skirt, sound, speech, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> spoken, talk, tenor, <sup><b><a href=\"#strongs-legend\">X</a></b></sup> to, two-edged, wish, word.";
