Lex["06439"] = "P@nuw'el {pen-oo-ale'} or (more properly,) P@niy'el {pen-oo-ale'}|AV - Penuel 8, Peniel 1; 9|from 06437 and 0410||noun proper masculine, noun proper locative| INDENT0--Penuel or Peniel = \"facing God\"<BR><br> INDENT0--noun proper masculine<BR>  INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a Benjamite, son of Shashak, brother of Iphedeiah of the family of Saul  INDENT0--<b>2)</b> son of Hur, father of Gedor, and a descendant of Judah<br><br>  INDENT0--noun proper locative<BR>  INDENT0--<b>3)</b> the place named by Jacob when he wrestled with God and located on the north bank of the Jabbok close to the Jordan <br /><BR /><hr /> INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><BR><BR> INDENT0--<span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1508;&#1468;&#1456;&#1504;&#1493;&#1468;&#1488;&#1461;&#1500; </span> P&#7497;n&#251;w&#700;&#234;l, pen-oo-ale&#39;; or (more properly,) <span style=\"font-size:150%\"> &#1508;&#1468;&#1456;&#1504;&#1460;&#1497;&#1488;&#1461;&#1500; </span> P&#x1D49;n&#xEE;y&#x2BC;&#xEA;l; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=6437&page=1\">H6437</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=410&page=1\">H410</a>; face of God; Penuel or Peniel, a place East of Jordan; also (as Penuel) the name of two Israelites:&#8212;Peniel, Penuel.";
